% Generate `tools/video/_shared.py`: shared helpers imported by the provider-specific
% video-generation tools (heygen_video, wan_video, hunyuan_video, ltx_video_local,
% ltx_video_modal, cogvideo_video, ...). It holds the model registries, cost/runtime
% estimators, the diffusers-based local generation path, the HeyGen + Modal API paths,
% image-upload helpers, and ffprobe/HDR inspection.
% Use `from __future__ import annotations`. Module-level imports: os, shutil, subprocess,
% time, pathlib(Path), typing(Any); `from tools.base_tool import ToolResult, ToolStatus`.
% Everything else (requests, torch, diffusers, PIL, base64, io, json) is imported lazily
% inside the function that needs it, so importing this module never requires the heavy stack.

## Model registries (module-level dicts, exact values — provider tools import these by name)

`HEYGEN_PROVIDERS` — HeyGen workflow `provider` string → `{name, quality, speed}`:
veo_3_1(Google VEO 3.1, highest, slow), veo_3_1_fast(Google VEO 3.1 Fast, high, medium),
veo3(Google VEO 3, high, slow), veo3_fast(Google VEO 3 Fast, high, medium),
veo2(Google VEO 2, medium, medium), kling_pro(Kling Pro, high, medium),
kling_v2(Kling v2, medium, fast), sora_v2(Sora v2, high, slow),
sora_v2_pro(Sora v2 Pro, highest, slow), runway_gen4(Runway Gen-4, high, medium),
seedance_lite(Seedance Lite (1.x), medium, fast), seedance_pro(Seedance Pro (1.x), high, medium),
ltx_distilled(LTX Distilled, low, fastest).
Add a NOTE comment on the seedance entries: HeyGen's `seedance_lite`/`seedance_pro` map to
Seedance 1.x; Seedance 2.0 is only via Video Agent / Avatar Shots endpoints (not the workflow
provider param) — for 2.0 use `seedance_video` (fal.ai) or `seedance_replicate`.

The four local-diffusers registries share the field set `{name, hf_id, [hf_i2v_id],
pipeline_class, vram_mb, quality, speed, t2v, i2v, license, default_width, default_height,
default_num_frames, fps}`:

`WAN_VARIANTS`:
- wan2.1-1.3b: Wan 2.1 (1.3B), hf_id Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-1.3B-Diffusers,
  hf_i2v_id Wan-AI/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P-Diffusers, WanPipeline, 8000, high, medium,
  t2v/i2v True, Apache-2.0, 832x480, 81 frames, 16 fps.
- wan2.1-14b: Wan 2.1 (14B), hf_id Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-14B-Diffusers,
  hf_i2v_id Wan-AI/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P-Diffusers, WanPipeline, 24000, highest, slow,
  t2v/i2v True, Apache-2.0, 1280x720, 81, 16.

`HUNYUAN_VARIANTS`:
- hunyuan-1.5: HunyuanVideo 1.5, hf_id tencent/HunyuanVideo-1.5, HunyuanVideoPipeline,
  14000, high, medium, t2v/i2v True, Apache-2.0, 848x480, 121, 24. (no hf_i2v_id)

`LTX_LOCAL_VARIANTS`:
- ltx2-local: LTX-2 (Local), hf_id Lightricks/LTX-2, LTXPipeline, 12000, high, medium,
  t2v/i2v True, LTX-2-Community, 768x512, 121, 24. (no hf_i2v_id)

`COGVIDEO_VARIANTS`:
- cogvideo-5b: CogVideoX 1.5 (5B), hf_id THUDM/CogVideoX-5b, CogVideoXPipeline, 12000,
  medium, medium, t2v/i2v True, Apache-2.0, 720x480, 49, 8.
- cogvideo-2b: CogVideoX (2B), hf_id THUDM/CogVideoX-2b, CogVideoXPipeline, 6000, medium,
  fast, t2v True / i2v False, Apache-2.0, 720x480, 49, 8.

`LTX2_FRAME_COUNTS` — duration hint → frame count: 1s 25, 2s 49, 3s 73, 4s 97, 5s 121,
6.7s 161, 8s 193.

## Gating + estimators

- `local_generation_enabled() -> bool`: env `VIDEO_GEN_LOCAL_ENABLED` in {true,1,yes} (lowercased).
- `local_generation_status() -> ToolStatus`: UNAVAILABLE unless enabled AND both `diffusers`
  and `torch` import; else AVAILABLE.
- `local_install_instructions() -> str`: tells the user to set `VIDEO_GEN_LOCAL_ENABLED=true`
  and `pip install diffusers transformers accelerate torch pillow requests`, on a GPU matching
  the tool's VRAM profile.
- `estimate_quality_cost(quality) -> float`: highest 0.50, high 0.35, low 0.15, else 0.20.
- `estimate_speed_runtime(speed) -> float`: fastest 30, fast 60, medium 120, slow 300, else 120.
- `estimate_local_runtime(speed) -> float`: fast 120, medium 240, slow 600, else 240.

## Local diffusers path

`load_diffusers_pipeline(pipeline_class, model_id, enable_offload)`: lazy-import diffusers+torch;
`getattr(diffusers, pipeline_class)`; dtype = bfloat16 if `torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported()` else
float16; `.from_pretrained(model_id, torch_dtype=dtype)`; if `enable_offload`
`enable_model_cpu_offload()` else `.to("cuda")`; if the pipe has a non-None `vae`, call
`enable_tiling()`/`enable_slicing()` when present; return the pipeline.

`load_reference_image(inputs, width, height)`: lazy-import io.BytesIO, requests, PIL.Image. Open
`reference_image_path` (convert RGB), else fetch `reference_image_url` (requests.get timeout 60,
raise_for_status, RGB), else return `ToolResult(success=False, error="image_to_video requires
reference_image_url or reference_image_path")`. On success return the image resized to
(width,height) with LANCZOS. (Callers must isinstance-check the result for ToolResult.)

`generate_local_video(*, tool_name, variants, default_variant, inputs) -> ToolResult`:
- variant = `inputs.get("model_variant", default_variant)`; if not in `variants` → error listing
  the sorted keys.
- meta = variants[variant]; prompt = `inputs["prompt"]`; operation = get("operation",
  "text_to_video"); seed = get("seed"); enable_offload = get("enable_model_offload", True).
- If operation is image_to_video but `meta["i2v"]` is falsy → error "{name} does not support
  image_to_video."
- width/height/num_frames from inputs falling back to the meta defaults; fps = meta["fps"].
- model_id = meta["hf_i2v_id"] when image_to_video AND that key exists, else meta["hf_id"].
- Build the pipeline via `load_diffusers_pipeline`. generation_args = prompt, num_frames, width,
  height, num_inference_steps=get("num_inference_steps", 30). If seed is not None add
  `generator = torch.Generator(device="cpu").manual_seed(seed)`. For image_to_video, load the
  reference image and return it if it's a ToolResult, else pass as `image`. For CogVideoXPipeline
  add `negative_prompt="worst quality, low quality, blurry, distorted, watermark"`.
- Run the pipeline; frames = `output.frames[0]` if it has `frames` else `output.images`.
- output_path = Path(get("output_path", f"{tool_name}_{variant}.mp4")); mkdir parents;
  `export_to_video(frames, str(output_path), fps=fps)` (from diffusers.utils).
- Return success ToolResult, data = provider(=tool_name), model_variant, provider_name(=name),
  mode "local", prompt, model_id, width, height, num_frames, fps,
  duration_seconds=round(num_frames/fps, 2), operation, output(str path), format "mp4", license,
  plus `**probe_output(output_path)`; artifacts=[path], seed=seed, model=model_id.

## HeyGen API path

`poll_heygen(execution_id, api_key, timeout=600) -> str`: poll GET
`https://api.heygen.com/v1/workflows/executions/{execution_id}` (header `X-Api-Key`) until a
deadline of now+timeout. Read `json()["data"]`; on status "completed" return
`data.output.video.video_url` or `data.output.video_url` (RuntimeError if neither); on status in
{failed, error} RuntimeError with `data.get("error","Unknown")`. Sleep with exponential backoff
starting 5s, ×1.2, capped 30s, and never past the deadline. TimeoutError if the deadline passes.

`upload_image_fal(image_path) -> str`: needs env `FAL_KEY` or `FAL_AI_API_KEY` (RuntimeError
otherwise); FileNotFoundError if the file is missing. content_type by extension (png→image/png,
jpg/jpeg→image/jpeg, webp→image/webp, default image/png). POST
`https://rest.alpha.fal.ai/storage/upload/initiate` (Authorization `Key {api_key}`, json
{content_type, file_name}); PUT the raw bytes to the returned `upload_url`; return `file_url`.

`upload_image_heygen(image_path, api_key) -> str`: FileNotFoundError if missing. First try HeyGen
v2 presigned upload: POST `https://api.heygen.com/v2/assets/upload` (X-Api-Key, json
{content_type image/png, file_name}); on 200 read `upload_url` and `url`/`file_url`, PUT the
bytes, return the file url. Swallow ANY exception from that branch and fall back to
`upload_image_fal(image_path)`.

`generate_heygen_video(inputs) -> ToolResult`: needs env `HEYGEN_API_KEY` (else error). provider =
get("provider_variant", "veo_3_1"); validate against HEYGEN_PROVIDERS (error listing sorted keys).
prompt = inputs["prompt"]; aspect_ratio = get("aspect_ratio", "16:9"); operation =
get("operation", "text_to_video"). workflow_input = {prompt, provider, aspect_ratio}; for
image_to_video resolve a `reference_image_url` — upload `reference_image_path` via
`upload_image_heygen` when only the path is given, error if neither, then add it to workflow_input.
POST `https://api.heygen.com/v1/workflows/executions` json {workflow_type "GenerateVideoNode",
input: workflow_input}; read `data.execution_id` (error if absent). `poll_heygen(...timeout=600)`,
then download the video (requests.get timeout 120) to output_path = Path(get("output_path",
f"heygen_video_{execution_id}.mp4")) (mkdir parents, write_bytes). Return success ToolResult, data
= provider "heygen", provider_variant, provider_name(=meta name), mode "api", prompt, aspect_ratio,
operation, execution_id, output, format "mp4"; artifacts=[path], model=provider.

## Modal LTX-2 API path

`generate_ltx_modal_video(inputs) -> ToolResult`: needs env `MODAL_LTX2_ENDPOINT_URL` (else error).
prompt, operation, aspect_ratio(default 16:9). width/height from inputs; if either is None derive
from aspect (16:9→1024x576, 9:16→576x1024, else 512x512). num_frames = get("num_frames",
LTX2_FRAME_COUNTS.get(get("duration_hint","5s"), 121)); if `(num_frames-1) % 8 != 0` snap it down
to the nearest `8n+1`. payload = prompt, width, height, num_frames, fps 24,
steps=get("num_inference_steps", 30), negative_prompt "worst quality, low quality, blurry,
distorted, watermark, text, logo"; add `seed` if given. For image_to_video: base64 the
`reference_image_path` bytes into `input_image`, else pass `reference_image_url` as
`input_image_url`, else error. POST the endpoint (timeout 300). Write output to Path(get(
"output_path","ltx_video_modal.mp4")): if the response content-type contains "video" or
"octet-stream" write bytes directly, else parse json for `video_url`/`url` (error if neither) and
download it (timeout 120). Return success ToolResult, data = provider "ltx-modal", provider_name
"LTX-2 (Modal)", mode "modal", prompt, width, height, num_frames, fps 24,
duration_seconds=round(num_frames/24, 2), operation, output, format "mp4"; artifacts=[path],
seed=get("seed"), model "ltx-2".

## ffprobe + HDR inspection

`probe_output(path) -> dict[str, Any]`: coerce to Path first (callers pass str or Path — note this
in a comment). Start with `file_size_bytes` from `path.stat().st_size`. If `shutil.which("ffprobe")`
is missing, return that alone. Otherwise run `ffprobe -v quiet -print_format json -show_format
-show_streams <path>` (capture, text, timeout 10, check False); on returncode 0 parse it and add
duration_seconds (float of format.duration or 0), file_size_mb (rounded MB), and from the first
video stream: video_width, video_height, video_codec, and the color metadata pix_fmt,
color_transfer, color_primaries, color_space (needed by `is_hdr_source` to avoid silently
tonemapping HDR). Swallow all exceptions and return whatever was gathered.

`is_hdr_source(path) -> dict[str, Any]`: detect HDR so callers never silently tonemap HDR→SDR.
Module constant `_HDR_TRANSFERS = {"arib-std-b67": "hlg", "smpte2084": "pq", "smpte-st-2084":
"pq"}`. Return the not-HDR default `{hdr False, kind None, transfer None, primaries None,
color_space None, pix_fmt None, bit_depth 8}` when the file is missing. Otherwise `probe_output`
it, lowercase color_transfer and pix_fmt, kind = `_HDR_TRANSFERS.get(transfer)`, bit_depth = 10
when pix_fmt contains any of "10le"/"10be"/"p010" else 8, and return {hdr: kind is not None, kind,
transfer or None, primaries, color_space, pix_fmt, bit_depth} pulling primaries/color_space/pix_fmt
from the probe (each `or None`). 10-bit + BT.2020 WITHOUT an HDR transfer is wide-gamut-not-HDR →
hdr False (never fabricate HDR from SDR).
